    {
      "id": "682d9175-44e6-4951-8248-1ca8ed6f0b62",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ChatGPT App\n\n* Go to your OpenAI profile (a Plus account is usually required).\n* Navigate to **Settings → Apps and Connectors → Advanced Settings**.\n* Enable **“Developer mode.”**\n* Go back to **Settings → Apps and Connectors** and click **“Create.”**\n* Set the MCP server URL from n8n (**“MCP Gmail Trigger”**).\n* Click **“Create.”**\n\n\n\n\n\n\n![image](https://n3wstorage.b-cdn.net/test/n8n-openaiagentbuilder.png)",
        "height": 832,
        "width": 912
      },
      "position": [
        -688,
        -240
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## OpenAI Agent Builder\n\n* Go to OpenAI’s [Agent Builder](https://platform.openai.com/agent-builder) and enable API.\n* Click **“Create a workflow.”**\n* Add an **Agent** node.\n* Open it and click the **“+”** button in the **Tools** section.\n* Select **“MCP Server.”**\n* Set the MCP server URL from n8n (**“MCP Gmail Trigger”**).\n* Click **“Create.”**\n* Click the **“+”** button again and set the MCP server URL from n8n (**“MCP Gmail Trigger”**).\n* Click **“Connect”** and **“Add”**\n\n![image](https://n3wstorage.b-cdn.net/test/n8n-chatgpt.png)",
        "height": 832,
        "width": 752
      },
      "position": [
        240,
        -240
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "962fdcbc-069a-47df-aba7-3d421ccd64d5",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "content": "## How to connect Google ecosystem with ChatGPT App & OpenAI Agent Builder (using MCP)\n\nThe official ChatGPT connector doesn’t allow you to interact directly with Google Workspace apps from within the app. Let’s see how to overcome this limitation by creating a dedicated **MCP server**.\n\nThis workflow acts as a **Middleware Control Point (MCP)** between **Google Workspace** services — including **Gmail, Drive, Docs, Sheets, Calendar, and Slides** — and **AI agents** like **OpenAI’s Agent Builder** and the **ChatGPT App**.\n\nIt enables these AI assistants to **directly interact with Google Workspace** tools — from managing emails and calendars to creating and editing documents, spreadsheets, or presentations — through secure automation endpoints, a feature that is not natively supported in the ChatGPT app.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 912
      },
      "position": [
        -688,
        -608
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
